# SNES Development Context

When working on assembly, patches, or ROM metadata in this repo:

1. Prefer the **gaia-snes** multi-root workspace (`c:/Work/gaia-snes.code-workspace`) so `gaia-knowledge` is indexed
2. Read `gaia-knowledge/curated/gaialabs/assembler-syntax.md` before editing `.asm`
3. IOG-specific docs: `docs/cop-commands-reference.md`, `docs/actor-organization-analysis.md` (also in knowledge corpus after ingest)
4. Rebuild to validate: `npm run rebuild`

## Label rules

`$&` = same-bank (2 bytes), `$@` = cross-bank (3 bytes). Do not guess.

## Database triad

- `us/blocks.json` — block/part structure (engine auto-discovers unmapped pieces)
- `us/overrides.json` — per-address register state and type corrections
- `us/names.json` — human-readable address labels

All three files are needed for the complete picture. See `gaia-knowledge/curated/gaialabs/reference-model.md`.

